WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.984
What you’re building, and who inherits it.

2
00:00:02.264 --> 00:00:13.869
The Studio 2 project is a question-answering system over a real, public document set: the Python PEPs, the Kubernetes documentation, a government handbook, or similar.

3
00:00:14.149 --> 00:00:22.661
A user asks a question, the system retrieves passages, and it answers with citations that your code has verified, or it says it doesn’t know.

4
00:00:22.941 --> 00:00:29.896
This lesson lays out one reasonable architecture, stage by stage, with the decision and the check at each stage.

5
00:00:30.176 --> 00:00:32.373
It deliberately doesn’t solve the project.

6
00:00:32.653 --> 00:00:43.192
The choices that matter most (how to chunk your corpus, which retrievers, what k, which model) depend on your documents, and the only honest way to make them is with measurements.

7
00:00:43.472 --> 00:00:48.144
One constraint shapes everything: this system is the patient for Studio 3.

8
00:00:48.424 --> 00:00:53.907
There you’ll build an evaluation harness, find failure modes systematically, and improve the system.

9
00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:58.112
That only works if the system you build now produces the right data.

10
00:00:58.392 --> 00:01:01.656
So design for being measured, starting with the eval set.
